ghpull:425 a bl:PullRequest, bl:WorkItem ;
    rdfs:label "rdf_owl_translator: return Err instead of panicking on try_get_individual, delete dead try_get_literal (#363)" ;
    bl:number 425 ;
    bl:state bl:Open .
# Note: no bl:closesIssue here. #363 is a long-running multi-PR tracking
# issue; this PR fixes try_get_individual/try_get_literal only. The final
# grep sweep found three panic sites still remaining in this crate
# (topological_sort's cycle detection, two "Multiple owl:members on
# owl:AllDisjointClasses/Properties" panics); those were fixed and merged
# separately as PR #424 while this branch was in flight, and this branch
# was rebased onto that merge. #363 also still has scope in other crates
# (datalog, eli2rl, rml) per the issue body. #363 stays open.

session:claudeSonnet5 a prov:SoftwareAgent ;
    rdfs:label "Claude Sonnet 5" .

session:pr425 a agp:AgentSession ;
    prov:wasAssociatedWith session:claudeSonnet5 ;
    prov:used ghissues:363 ;
    prov:startedAtTime "2026-08-08T14:45:55Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-08-08T14:53:36Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

session:pr425Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Issue #363 is a long-running effort to stop the crate from panic!()-ing the whole --serve process on malformed-but-parseable ontology input; this PR is its eighth cluster, scoped to try_get_individual and try_get_literal in rdf_owl_translator/src/ingress.rs. try_get_individual panicked whenever a graph element expected to denote an OWL individual (owl:NamedIndividual subject, owl:sameAs individuals, owl:oneOf members, owl:hasValue's object-property arm) turned out to be a literal or an RDF 1.2 triple term. Its 7 call sites split into two structurally different shapes, requiring two different fixes rather than one uniform Result-threading pass: the 5 sites in axiom_parser.rs already sit inside Result-returning functions (extract_axiom and siblings), so try_get_individual's signature was changed to Result<Individual, TranslatorError> and those sites just added `?`. The 2 sites in class_expression_parser.rs (owl:oneOf, owl:hasValue) sit inside ClassExprBuilder closures -- Box<dyn Fn(...) -> ClassExpression> -- which are not Result-returning and are shared by every anonymous class-expression kind in the file; changing that closure type to thread Result through would have been a much larger refactor with no scope boundary of its own, so instead of forcing the type change we followed the precedent PR #400 already set for the structurally identical owl:hasSelf/try_get_bool_literal case: log::warn! and a non-fatal fallback. owl:oneOf skips just the malformed member rather than aborting the whole restriction (an ObjectOneOf missing one bad member is more useful than none), with an added edge case caught during review: if filtering leaves zero members, that's not 'fine, smaller list' but a silent change to the empty class, so it now falls back to owl:Thing the same way owl:hasValue's malformed case does. try_get_literal was deleted rather than converted -- a fresh grep found zero call sites anywhere in the workspace, so there was nothing to convert for; CLAUDE.md's dead-code convention says delete outright. The final panic!/unwrap()/expect() sweep of rdf_owl_translator/src/ found three sites still remaining (topological_sort's cycle-detection panic, and two 'Multiple owl:members on owl:AllDisjointClasses/Properties' panics) -- cross-checking against origin/main and gh pr diff showed these were exactly the scope of PR #424, then open and unmerged, so they were deliberately left alone here to avoid duplicating in-flight work rather than being additional findings. #424 merged into main while this branch was still open; this branch was subsequently rebased onto that merge (resolving conflicts in error.rs's TranslatorError enum, which both PRs extended, and additive-only conflicts in the test files) rather than left to rot. #363 stays open and this PR carries no bl:closesIssue triple." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:425 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr425 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 ;
    agp:decisionPoint session:pr425Decision .

session:pr425Decision a agp:Decision ;
    agp:summaryText "For the 2 class_expression_parser.rs call sites, chose log::warn!-and-fallback inside the existing non-Result ClassExprBuilder closure type, mirroring PR #400's owl:hasSelf precedent exactly (skip-and-warn for owl:oneOf members, fall back to owl:Thing for owl:hasValue and for an all-malformed owl:oneOf)." ;
    agp:alternative "Considered threading Result through ClassExprBuilder (Box<dyn Fn(&OntologyDeclarations, &X) -> Result<ClassExpression, TranslatorError>>) for full symmetry with the axiom_parser.rs call sites. Rejected: that closure type is used for every anonymous class-expression kind in class_expression_parser.rs, not just these two, so the change would have touched a large, unrelated surface area for a fix scoped to 2 call sites -- disproportionate to this PR's actual scope and explicitly called out as out-of-scope in the task brief." .
